HALT switch for the SENTINEL cloud scanner.

If a file named HALT (exactly that name, no extension) exists in the repo
root, the scanner does nothing except write the heartbeat. No paper trades,
no exit checks, no fire.

To stop the scanner:   copy this file to a new file named HALT and commit it.
To start it again:     delete the HALT file and commit.

The content of the HALT file does not matter. Only its presence counts.
While HALT is present, state/heartbeat.json shows status "HALT".
